------------------
Known issues/notes
------------------
- flite's internal resampler (used when 'samplerate' differs from the chosen
  voice's native rate) performs an overlapping memcpy (undefined behaviour,
  reported upstream) and pads each resampled prompt with ~110-250ms of
  trailing silence, which also ends up in cached files. Prefer voice/rate
  combinations that need no resampling (kal at 8000, kal16 at 16000).
- flite's G.721 voice-data decoder contains benign undefined behaviour
  (negative left shifts); reported upstream.
- On out-of-memory flite terminates the calling process by design
  (cst_error/exit). The 'maxtext' limit bounds the realistic trigger.
- Do NOT force-unload this module ("module unload -f") while calls are using
  it: in-flight calls can crash Asterisk. A normal unload is safe.
